    "name": "Purple Radish",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Purple radishes, often found as varieties like the purple daikon (Bora King, KN-Bravo), are&nbsp;crisp, mild, and slightly sweet root vegetables, commonly used raw in salads or pickled. They have violet skin with a white, purple-streaked interior, offering a crunchy texture and high levels of anthocyanins, antioxidants, Vitamin C, and fiber.</span></p>",
